IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg6-s251a-agreement`
IMPORT `dg6-s251f-no-vote`
IMPORT `dg6-s251h-tender-offer`
IMPORT `dg6-s252-foreign-corporation`
IMPORT `dg6-s253-parent-subsidiary`
IMPORT `dg6-s254-joint-stock`
IMPORT `dg6-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer dg6-seat.l4 (8 Del. C. §§ 251 to 254): at least one case for each of its questions, with the
-- facts a person in the seat would state. Every expected value was written by hand from the text of the section
-- (de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, lines 1061-1169) before the file was run; a failing assertion is a finding, and none was edited.
-- A case outside the encoding returns NOTHING (the Law's silence, never a "no"), and is asserted as such.
-- The fee under section 391(a)(29) is dg11's; the 35 dollars below is an assumed input, not the figure of the Law.

`the merger kind` MEANS `a merger into a single surviving corporation`
`the consolidation kind` MEANS `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation`
`parent merges subs into itself` MEANS `the parent corporation merges the subsidiary corporation or corporations into itself and assumes all of its or their obligations`
`parent merges into a sub` MEANS `the parent corporation merges itself, or itself and one or more of the other subsidiary corporations, into one of the subsidiary corporations`

§ `Cases for the questions of dg6-seat.l4`

§§ `s 251(a) and (b)`

-- A director: two Delaware corporations merge, one survives, the agreement complies and is approved.
#ASSERT `s 251(a) May our corporation merge or consolidate with another corporation of this State` `the merger kind` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A stockholder told that only one of the combining corporations is a Delaware corporation: section 251(a) needs two or more.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(a) May our corporation merge or consolidate with another corporation of this State` `the merger kind` 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- An incorporator: three corporations consolidate into a new one.
#ASSERT `s 251(a) May our corporation merge or consolidate with another corporation of this State` `the consolidation kind` 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- A director of a corporation that desires to merge: the board must adopt the resolution (section 251(b)).
#ASSERT `s 251(b) Must our board adopt a resolution approving the agreement and declaring its advisability` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(b) Must our board adopt a resolution approving the agreement and declaring its advisability` FALSE)
-- The board approved the agreement but did not declare it advisable: it has not done what the subsection requires.
#ASSERT `s 251(b) Has our board adopted the resolution the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(b) Has our board adopted the resolution the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE)
-- A merger agreement that states the terms and mode and the survivor's certificate, converts and cancels nothing, has no
-- cash in lieu, is signed by an authorized person and is not filed: compliant. The kind, then the 14 facts in the order asked.
#ASSERT `s 251(b) Does our merger agreement comply with the subsection` `the merger kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- The same agreement, but some shares are to be converted and it does not say how: not compliant (section 251(b)(5)).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(b) Does our merger agreement comply with the subsection` `the merger kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Holders of shares that do not remain outstanding are to receive cash of another corporation, and the agreement says so: compliant.
#ASSERT `s 251(b) Does our merger agreement comply with the subsection` `the merger kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(b) May a term of our merger agreement depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(b) May a term of our merger agreement depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` FALSE)
-- A director: a term that turns on the board's own determination (a determination or action by a person or body) depends on a fact; a term that turns on something the sentence does not name: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `s 251(b) Is what the term of our merger agreement depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` `an event, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(b) Is what the term of our merger agreement depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` `a determination or action by a person or body, including the corporation, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(b) Is what the term of our merger agreement depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` `something else, which the facts sentence of s 251(b) neither names nor excludes` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 251(c)`

-- A minority holder of non-voting stock is owed notice too.
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Am I entitled to notice of the meeting on the merger` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(c) Am I entitled to notice of the meeting on the merger` FALSE)
-- Meeting on 1 March 2026: notice by 9 February 2026 (20 days before).
#ASSERT `s 251(c) By what date must notice of the meeting on the merger be given` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 9
-- A stockholder who got notice on 9 February 2026 of a meeting on 1 March, with the address, time, place, purpose and a summary.
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Was the notice of the meeting on the merger due notice` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 9) TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Notice given on 10 February is 19 days before the meeting: not due notice.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(c) Was the notice of the meeting on the merger due notice` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Does the merger agreement have to be put to a vote of our stockholders` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(c) Does the merger agreement have to be put to a vote of our stockholders` TRUE)
-- 5,100 of 10,000 votes: a majority. 5,000 is not more than half.
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement` `a stock corporation` 5100 10000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement` `a stock corporation` 5000 10000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A nonstock corporation: not covered by section 251's stockholder vote (section 114(b)(2)).
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` 60 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A certificate requiring 66 2/3% (section 102(b)(4)), entered as the fraction 2/3: 600 of 900 votes is exactly two thirds and reaches it;
-- 599 does not. (A decimal 66.67 would have asked for 600.03 votes: the question takes a numerator and a denominator for that reason.)
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement by the larger vote our certificate requires` `a stock corporation` 2 3 FALSE 600 900 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement by the larger vote our certificate requires` `a stock corporation` 2 3 FALSE 599 900 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A denominator of 0 is not a fraction: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement by the larger vote our certificate requires` `a stock corporation` 2 0 FALSE 600 900 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A certificate requiring 75% (section 102(b)(4)): 7,500 of 10,000 reaches it; 7,499 does not; a bare majority would not do.
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement by the larger vote our certificate requires` `a stock corporation` 3 4 FALSE 7500 10000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement by the larger vote our certificate requires` `a stock corporation` 3 4 FALSE 7499 10000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Did our stockholders adopt the merger agreement by the larger vote our certificate requires` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` 3 4 FALSE 8000 10000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The secretary: adopted by a majority, no certificate in lieu: must certify. With a certificate in lieu: need not.
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Must the secretary or assistant secretary certify the adoption on the agreement` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(c) Must the secretary or assistant secretary certify the adoption on the agreement` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Must the merger agreement now be filed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(c) Must the merger agreement now be filed` FALSE)
-- A certificate of merger with all seven statements and executed per section 103.
#ASSERT `s 251(c) Does our certificate of merger or consolidation state what the subsection requires` `the merger kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A certificate that omits the statement that a copy will be furnished free on request.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(c) Does our certificate of merger or consolidation state what the subsection requires` `the merger kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A stockholder of a constituent corporation, a certificate having been filed in lieu of the agreement: may ask for a copy.
#ASSERT `s 251(c)(7) Can I as a stockholder get a copy of the merger agreement without cost` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(c)(7) Can I as a stockholder get a copy of the merger agreement without cost` FALSE TRUE)
-- Our corporation: board resolution adopted, 5,100 of 10,000 votes, no exemption: approved.
#ASSERT `s 251(a) Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 251 requires` `a stock corporation` TRUE 5100 10000 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(a) Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 251 requires` `a stock corporation` FALSE 5100 10000 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No vote was held (0 of 10,000) but the merger is exempt under (f), (g) or (h): approved.
#ASSERT `s 251(a) Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 251 requires` `a stock corporation` TRUE 0 10000 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A vote that cannot be counted (more votes than the stock carries), no exemption: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 251(a) Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 251 requires` `a stock corporation` TRUE 12000 10000 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 251(d) and (e)`

#ASSERT `s 251(d) May our board terminate the merger agreement` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(d) May our board terminate the merger agreement` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(d) May our board terminate the merger agreement` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 251(d) Must a certificate of termination be filed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(d) Must a certificate of termination be filed` FALSE TRUE)
-- Amendment, after our stockholders adopted: nothing in (1) to (3) altered: allowed. Inputs: provision, not yet effective, then ours (adopted, consideration, adverse), the other's (adopted, consideration, adverse), survivor's certificate altered.
#ASSERT `s 251(d) May the boards amend the merger agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- It alters what our holders receive after we adopted: barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(d) May the boards amend the merger agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The other corporation's stockholders have not voted and the amendment alters what its holders receive: allowed.
#ASSERT `s 251(d) May the boards amend the merger agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Our stockholders adopted and the amendment alters the survivor's certificate: barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(d) May the boards amend the merger agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 251(d) Must a certificate of amendment be filed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(d) Must a certificate of amendment be filed` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 251(e) Is the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation automatically amended` `the merger kind` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(e) Is the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation automatically amended` `the merger kind` FALSE)

§§ `s 251(f)`

-- We survive, our certificate does not require a vote and is not amended, every share is identical, and 100 + 100 = 200 shares
-- are issued or issuable against 1,000 outstanding: exactly 20%, which "do[es] not exceed 20%".
#ASSERT `s 251(f) Is our merger exempt from a vote of our stockholders because we survive it and change nothing` `the merger kind` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 100 100 1000
-- 201 of 1,000 exceeds 20%.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(f) Is our merger exempt from a vote of our stockholders because we survive it and change nothing` `the merger kind` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 101 100 1000)
#ASSERT `s 251(f) Is our merger exempt from a vote of our stockholders because we have issued no stock` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(f) Is our merger exempt from a vote of our stockholders because we have issued no stock` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 251(f) Is a vote of our stockholders unnecessary under either sentence` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 251(f) Is a vote of our stockholders unnecessary under either sentence` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(f) Is a vote of our stockholders unnecessary under either sentence` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 251(f) What must the secretary or assistant secretary certify on the agreement` TRUE `the first sentence of s 251(f)` FALSE EQUALS `that the agreement has been adopted pursuant to s 251(f) and that the conditions specified in its first sentence have been satisfied`
#ASSERT `s 251(f) What must the secretary or assistant secretary certify on the agreement` TRUE `the second sentence of s 251(f)` FALSE EQUALS `that the agreement has been adopted pursuant to s 251(f) and that no shares of stock were issued before the board adopted the resolution approving the agreement`
#ASSERT `s 251(f) What must the secretary or assistant secretary certify on the agreement` TRUE `the second sentence of s 251(f)` TRUE EQUALS `nothing, because the agreement was not adopted under s 251(f) without a vote of the stockholders, or a certificate is filed in lieu of the agreement`
#ASSERT `s 251(f) Does my executing the agreement represent that the certified facts remain true` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(f) Does my executing the agreement represent that the certified facts remain true` FALSE)

§§ `s 251(g)`

-- A holding-company merger: every condition (1) to (8) met, the surviving entity a limited liability company with the
-- provisions (7)(A) and (B) require, the board having determined no gain or loss to the stockholders.
#ASSERT `s 251(g) Can our corporation merge into its wholly-owned subsidiary without a vote of our stockholders` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The same, but the board has not made the tax determination of paragraph (8).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(g) Can our corporation merge into its wholly-owned subsidiary without a vote of our stockholders` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The same, but our certificate expressly requires a vote.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(g) Can our corporation merge into its wholly-owned subsidiary without a vote of our stockholders` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 251(g) Is the corporation a holding company` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(g) Is the corporation a holding company` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(i) Do the section 203 restrictions still apply to the holding company and its stockholders` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(i) Do the section 203 restrictions still apply to the holding company and its stockholders` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(i) From what date are my holding company shares treated as acquired for section 203` (YearMonthDay 2019 5 17) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 5 17
-- I was not an interested stockholder before: the merger alone does not make me one.
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(i) Does the merger by itself make me an interested stockholder of the holding company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I already was one: the proviso says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(i) Does the merger by itself make me an interested stockholder of the holding company` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(ii) Do my old stock certificates represent shares of the holding company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(ii) Do my old stock certificates represent shares of the holding company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(iii) Do I keep standing to bring or maintain a derivative suit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(iii) Do I keep standing to bring or maintain a derivative suit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 251(g) What are the organizational documents of the surviving entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the certificate of incorporation of a corporation`
#ASSERT `s 251(g) What are the organizational documents of the surviving entity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the limited liability company agreement of a limited liability company`
#ASSERT `s 251(g) What are the organizational documents of the surviving entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(7) Does the required provision let the holding company's stockholders approve electing or removing directors or managers` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 251(g)(7) Does the required provision let the holding company's stockholders approve electing or removing directors or managers` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 251(g) Must the secretary or assistant secretary certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(g)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(g) Must the secretary or assistant secretary certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(g)` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 251(g) Does my executing the agreement represent that the certified facts remain true` TRUE

§§ `s 251(h)`

-- More than 2,000 holders of record qualifies; exactly 2,000 does not; a listed class qualifies at any number.
#ASSERT `s 251(h) Is our corporation listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` FALSE 2001
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(h) Is our corporation listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` FALSE 2000)
#ASSERT `s 251(h) Is our corporation listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` TRUE 12
-- The tally for all the stock: 1,000 votes; 400 accepted and received + 100 otherwise owned = 500, not more than half.
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(3) Do the shares held after the offer reach the vote that would have been required` 1000 400 100 0 1 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(3) Do the shares held after the offer reach the vote that would have been required` 1000 401 100 0 1 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A certificate requiring 66 2/3% (the fraction 2/3): of 900 votes that is exactly 600; 500 received + 100 otherwise owned reaches it, 499 + 100 does not.
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(3) Do the shares held after the offer reach the vote that would have been required` 900 500 100 0 2 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(3) Do the shares held after the offer reach the vote that would have been required` 900 499 100 0 2 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(3) Do the shares held after the offer reach the vote that would have been required` 900 500 100 0 2 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A certificate requiring "at least 90%": 900 of 1,000 reaches it.
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(3) Do the shares held after the offer reach the vote that would have been required` 1000 800 0 100 9 10 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Counts that cannot be a vote: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(3) Do the shares held after the offer reach the vote that would have been required` 1000 900 300 0 1 2 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- All conditions of paragraphs (1) to (5) met, with the 2,001 holders: no vote needed.
#ASSERT `s 251(h) Can the merger go ahead without a vote of our stockholders after a tender offer` FALSE 2001 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The offer was not consummated for all the voting stock: the exemption fails.
#ASSERT `s 251(h) Can the merger go ahead without a vote of our stockholders after a tender offer` FALSE 2001 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Only 2,000 holders and not listed: the corporation cannot use the subsection at all.
#ASSERT `s 251(h) Can the merger go ahead without a vote of our stockholders after a tender offer` FALSE 2000 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Excluded stock: stock the offeror owned when the offer began.
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(6)d. Is my stock excluded stock` `owned by the corporation making the offer at the commencement of the offer` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(h)(6)d. Is my stock excluded stock` `owned by some other holder at the commencement of the offer` FALSE)
-- My shares are rollover stock: they are excluded stock even though I am some other holder.
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(6)d. Is my stock excluded stock` `owned by some other holder at the commencement of the offer` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(6)a. Is the person an affiliate of the corporation making the offer` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(h)(6)a. Is the person an affiliate of the corporation making the offer` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- My certificated shares: certificate and letter of transmittal delivered, certificate not canceled: received.
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(6)f. Are my tendered shares received` `certificated shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(h)(6)f. Are my tendered shares received` `certificated shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(6)g. Are my shares rollover stock` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(h)(6)g. Are my shares rollover stock` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 251(h)(6)g. Are my shares still rollover stock for the tender-offer count` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(h)(6)g. Are my shares still rollover stock for the tender-offer count` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 251(h) Must the secretary or assistant secretary certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(h)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251(h) Must the secretary or assistant secretary certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(h)` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 251(h) Does my executing the agreement represent that the certified facts remain true` TRUE

§§ `s 252`

-- A Delaware corporation merges into a Nevada corporation, which survives; Nevada law does not prohibit it. Inputs: kind, Delaware
-- constituents, foreign constituents, foreign law prohibits, survivor is a constituent, resulting corporation of a constituent's jurisdiction, complies, approved.
#ASSERT `s 252(a) May our corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation` `the merger kind` 1 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(a) May our corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation` `the merger kind` 1 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- The agreement with a foreign corporation whose survivor is a Delaware corporation: the kind, survivor is Delaware, then 13 facts.
#ASSERT `s 252(b) Does our agreement with a foreign corporation comply with the subsection` `the merger kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- It omits what the foreign jurisdiction's law requires it to state.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(b) Does our agreement with a foreign corporation comply with the subsection` `the merger kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 252(b) May a term of our agreement with a foreign corporation depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(b) May a term of our agreement with a foreign corporation depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` FALSE)
-- The same sentence in section 252(b), read the same way.
#ASSERT `s 252(b) Is what the term of our agreement with a foreign corporation depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` `an event, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 252(b) Is what the term of our agreement with a foreign corporation depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` `a determination or action by a person or body, including the corporation, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 252(b) Is what the term of our agreement with a foreign corporation depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` `something else, which the facts sentence of s 251(b) neither names nor excludes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Our corporation is a Delaware corporation: adopted under its own law, board resolution, 5,100 of 10,000 votes, no exemption.
#ASSERT `s 252(c) Has our corporation adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE 5100 10000 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 252(c) Has our corporation adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE 5000 10000 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A foreign constituent: only its own law.
#ASSERT `s 252(c) Has our corporation adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 252(c) When does the agreement become effective for all purposes of the laws of this State` (YearMonthDay 2027 6 30) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 6 30
-- The certificate, a merger whose survivor is a Nevada corporation: no statement of the survivor's certificate; the (d) agreement is needed.
#ASSERT `s 252(c) Does our certificate of merger with a foreign corporation state what the subsection requires` `the merger kind` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(c) Does our certificate of merger with a foreign corporation state what the subsection requires` `the merger kind` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 252(c)(7) Can I as a stockholder get a copy of the agreement with a foreign corporation without cost` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(c)(7) Can I as a stockholder get a copy of the agreement with a foreign corporation without cost` TRUE FALSE)
-- Service of process on a foreign survivor.
#ASSERT `s 252(d) Is the surviving or resulting corporation a foreign corporation that must agree to be served in this State` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Is the surviving or resulting corporation a foreign corporation that must agree to be served in this State` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 252(d) Has the foreign surviving corporation given the agreement the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Has the foreign surviving corporation given the agreement the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- As a plaintiff enforcing an appraisal award against the Nevada survivor.
#ASSERT `s 252(d) Can I serve the foreign surviving corporation through the Secretary of State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Can I serve the foreign surviving corporation through the Secretary of State` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Can I serve the foreign surviving corporation through the Secretary of State` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 252(d) May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 252(d) May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Service by other means: the sentence says nothing about it.
#ASSERT `s 252(d) May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 252(d) Have I as plaintiff done everything the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE 35 35
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Have I as plaintiff done everything the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE 30 35)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Have I as plaintiff done everything the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE 35 35)
#ASSERT `s 252(d) How much must the plaintiff pay the Secretary of State` 35 EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `s 252(d) Is the fee taxed as part of the costs` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Is the fee taxed as part of the costs` FALSE)
-- From the survivor's side.
#ASSERT `s 252(d) Must the Secretary of State notify us of the service` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Must the Secretary of State notify us of the service` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 252(d) To what address will the Secretary of State mail the letter` FALSE EQUALS `the address specified in the agreement for mailing a copy of the process`
#ASSERT `s 252(d) To what address will the Secretary of State mail the letter` TRUE EQUALS `the last address that the corporation designated in writing to the Secretary of State for the purpose`
#ASSERT `s 252(d) Is the Secretary of State's letter sent as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Is the Secretary of State's letter sent as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 252(d) Does the Secretary of State's record of the service contain what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) Does the Secretary of State's record of the service contain what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Retention: service received 1 March 2026; on 1 March 2031 (5 years) the record is still kept; on 2 March 2031 it need not be.
#ASSERT `s 252(d) On the date asked about, must the Secretary of State still keep the record` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2031 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(d) On the date asked about, must the Secretary of State still keep the record` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2031 3 2))
#ASSERT `s 252(e) Does section 251(d) apply to our merger or consolidation with a foreign corporation` `the merger kind`
#ASSERT `s 252(e) Does section 251(d) apply to our merger or consolidation with a foreign corporation` `the consolidation kind`
#ASSERT `s 252(e) Does section 251(e) apply to our merger with a foreign corporation` `the merger kind` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(e) Does section 251(e) apply to our merger with a foreign corporation` `the merger kind` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 252(e) Do section 251(f) and (h) apply to our merger with a foreign corporation` `the merger kind`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252(e) Do section 251(f) and (h) apply to our merger with a foreign corporation` `the consolidation kind`)

§§ `s 253`

-- The parent owns 95 of 100 votes of the class it holds least of; that class votes; no holding-company provision;
-- one of the corporations is Delaware; no foreign prohibition: it may merge us.
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Can the parent corporation merge us into itself or itself into us` 100 95 TRUE FALSE 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 90 of 100 is enough ("at least 90%"); 89 is not.
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Can the parent corporation merge us into itself or itself into us` 100 90 TRUE FALSE 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Can the parent corporation merge us into itself or itself into us` 100 89 TRUE FALSE 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Our certificate carries the holding-company provision of section 251(g)(7): outside section 253.
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Can the parent corporation merge us into itself or itself into us` 100 95 TRUE TRUE 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Owned votes exceed the votes of the class: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Can the parent corporation merge us into itself or itself into us` 100 120 TRUE FALSE 2 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Does the certificate of ownership and merger state what the subsection requires` `parent merges subs into itself` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- The parent is a Delaware corporation merging into the subsidiary: the certificate must state its stockholders' approval.
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Does the certificate of ownership and merger state what the subsection requires` `parent merges into a sub` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(a) Does the certificate of ownership and merger state what the subsection requires` `parent merges into a sub` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A minority holder: the parent owns 95%; its board resolution must state what I get for my shares.
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Does the parent's board resolution state what the subsection requires` `parent merges subs into itself` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(a) Does the parent's board resolution state what the subsection requires` `parent merges subs into itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 253(a) May a term of the resolution depend on facts ascertainable outside the resolution` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(a) May a term of the resolution depend on facts ascertainable outside the resolution` FALSE)
-- The same sentence in section 253(a), read the same way.
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Is what the term of the resolution depends on a fact within the sentence on the resolution` `an event, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Is what the term of the resolution depends on a fact within the sentence on the resolution` `a determination or action by a person or body, including the corporation, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Is what the term of the resolution depends on a fact within the sentence on the resolution` `something else, which the facts sentence of s 251(b) neither names nor excludes` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Did the parent's stockholders approve the merger by the required vote` `a stock corporation` 5100 10000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Did the parent's stockholders approve the merger by the required vote` `a stock corporation` 5000 10000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A nonstock parent that does not survive: section 253(e) applies the section to a nonstock parent only if it survives.
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Did the parent's stockholders approve the merger by the required vote` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` 60 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 253(a) By what date must notice of the meeting of the parent's stockholders be given` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 9
#ASSERT `s 253(a) Was the meeting of the parent's stockholders held after the notice the subsection requires` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 9) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(a) Was the meeting of the parent's stockholders held after the notice the subsection requires` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 253(a)(1) Which section also applies where the surviving corporation is foreign` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `section 252(d)`
#ASSERT `s 253(a)(1) Which section also applies where the surviving corporation is foreign` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `section 258(c)`
#ASSERT `s 253(a)(1) Which section also applies where the surviving corporation is foreign` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 253(a)(2) Must the terms of the merger obligate the foreign surviving corporation` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(a)(2) Must the terms of the merger obligate the foreign surviving corporation` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 253(b) May the surviving corporation change its corporate name` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(b) May the surviving corporation change its corporate name` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 253(b) Has the name of the surviving corporation changed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(b) Has the name of the surviving corporation changed` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 253(c) Does section 251(d) apply to the section 253 merger` `parent merges subs into itself`
#ASSERT `s 253(c) Does section 251(d) apply to the section 253 merger` `parent merges into a sub`
#ASSERT `s 253(c) Does section 251(e) apply to the section 253 merger` `parent merges into a sub` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(c) Does section 251(e) apply to the section 253 merger` `parent merges subs into itself` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 253(c) What does agreement of merger mean in a section 253 merger` EQUALS `the resolution of merger adopted by the board of directors of the parent corporation`
#ASSERT `s 253(c) Must the merger be done under another section` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(c) Must the merger be done under another section` FALSE)
-- A minority holder: the parent does not own all the stock, so section 262 applies and I have appraisal rights as set forth in it.
#ASSERT `s 253(c) Does section 262 apply to the section 253 merger` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(c) Does section 262 apply to the section 253 merger` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 253(d) Do I have appraisal rights as a stockholder of the subsidiary` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(d) Do I have appraisal rights as a stockholder of the subsidiary` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 253(e) Does section 253 apply to our nonstock parent` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(e) Does section 253 apply to our nonstock parent` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 253(e) Are references to the parent's directors and board read as its governing body` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 253(e) Are references to the parent's directors and board read as its governing body` `a stock corporation` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 253(f) Does section 253 authorize the merger with the charitable nonstock corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 253(f) Does section 253 authorize the merger with the charitable nonstock corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 254`

-- A trust with unit holders is a joint-stock association; so is one commonly known as such; a limited liability company is not.
#ASSERT `s 254(a) Is the body a joint-stock association for the purposes of section 254` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 254(a) Is the body a joint-stock association for the purposes of section 254` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 254(a) Is the body a joint-stock association for the purposes of section 254` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 254(a) Is the body a joint-stock association for the purposes of section 254` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 254(a) Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 254` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 254(a) Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 254` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 254(a) Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 254` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 254(b) May the entity be the surviving or resulting entity` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 254(b) May the entity be the surviving or resulting entity` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 254(b) May the entity be the surviving or resulting entity` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A Delaware corporation merges into a joint-stock association; the law of the association's jurisdiction does not prohibit it.
#ASSERT `s 254(b) May our corporation merge or consolidate with a joint-stock association` `the merger kind` 1 1 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 254(b) May our corporation merge or consolidate with a joint-stock association` `the merger kind` 1 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 254(c) Does our agreement with a joint-stock association comply with the subsection` `the merger kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 254(c) Does our agreement with a joint-stock association comply with the subsection` `the merger kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 254(c) May a term of our agreement with a joint-stock association depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 254(c) May a term of our agreement with a joint-stock association depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` FALSE)
-- The same sentence in section 254(c), read the same way.
#ASSERT `s 254(c) Is what the term of our agreement with a joint-stock association depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` `an event, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 254(c) Is what the term of our agreement with a joint-stock association depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` `a determination or action by a person or body, including the corporation, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 254(c) Is what the term of our agreement with a joint-stock association depends on a fact within the closing paragraph` `something else, which the facts sentence of s 251(b) neither names nor excludes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Our constituent entity is a stock corporation: board resolution, 5,100 of 10,000 votes. A nonstock corporation: as section 255 provides (a yes/no here).
#ASSERT `s 254(d) Has our constituent entity adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires` `a stock corporation constituent of the merger or consolidation` TRUE 5100 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 254(d) Has our constituent entity adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires` `a nonstock corporation constituent of the merger or consolidation` FALSE 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 254(d) Has our constituent entity adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires` `a joint-stock association constituent of the merger or consolidation` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 254(d) Has our constituent entity adopted and approved the agreement as the subsection requires` `a stock corporation constituent of the merger or consolidation` TRUE 12000 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 254(d) When does the agreement become effective for all purposes of the laws of this State` (YearMonthDay 2028 1 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2028 1 31
-- A certificate whose survivor is a Delaware corporation: kind, survivor is Delaware, survivor is an association formed elsewhere, then 9 facts.
#ASSERT `s 254(d) Does our certificate of merger with a joint-stock association state what the subsection requires` `the merger kind` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
